---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import config from "../../site.config.mjs";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/")
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
const contact = `${base}contact/`;
const updated = "July 27, 2026";
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description={`The terms governing use of ${config.name}.`}>
  <section class="section container guide-detail">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="guide-meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of mississaugainsider.ca, operated by {config.name} ("we", "us"). By
        using the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What the site is</h2>
      <p>
        {config.name} is an informational site covering {config.city}, {config.province}: curated local
        news headlines, event listings, a business directory, and original <a href={`${base}guides/`}>Guides</a>
        and <a href={`${base}spotlight/`}>Business Spotlight</a> articles. See our
        <a href={`${base}about/`}>About page</a> for how we source and credit content.
      </p>

      <h2>News content</h2>
      <p>
        News items on the site are short excerpts, headline and a brief summary, with credit and a link to
        the original publisher. We do not republish full articles, and we are not the author of the outlets
        we credit. For the complete story, follow the link to the original source.
      </p>

      <h2>Business directory</h2>
      <p>
        Directory listings are compiled from public Google Maps Platform data, not verified by us for current
        accuracy. Hours, contact details, and other information can change without notice, so confirm
        directly with the business before visiting. If you're a business owner and want a listing corrected
        or removed, <a href={contact}>contact us</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Paid placements (a Directory Priority Listing, a Featured or VIP Business Spotlight, newsletter
        sponsorship, or a display ad) are separate arrangements between the advertiser and {config.name},
        agreed to individually and not covered in detail by these general terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Events and guides</h2>
      <p>
        Event listings are pulled from public calendars and may change or be cancelled by the organizer
        without notice. Guides are original, evergreen explainers; details like hours, admission, or
        seasonal availability can change after publication, so treat them as a starting point rather than
        a guarantee.
      </p>

      <h2>Referral program</h2>
      <p>
        From time to time we run promotions, such as a reward for recommending a business that goes on to be
        featured in a Business Spotlight. Any such promotion is offered at our discretion, including who
        qualifies and how a reward is paid out, and can be changed or ended at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Don't misuse the site, the contact form, or any promotion to submit false, abusive, or fraudulent
        information, or to attempt to disrupt or gain unauthorized access to the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links and embeds</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to and, on some pages, embeds content from third-party services (including Beehiiv,
        GoHighLevel, YouTube, Instagram, and the original publishers we credit in news items). We aren't
        responsible for the content, availability, or practices of those third-party services.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided "as is." We make reasonable efforts to keep it accurate and available, but we
        don't guarantee it will be error-free, uninterrupted, or fit for any particular purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, {config.name} is not liable for any damages arising from your use of,
        or inability to use, the site, including reliance on information found here.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario, Canada.</p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top will always reflect
        the most recent version.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? <a href={contact}>Contact us</a>. See also our
        <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
